        "faq_0": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "My GPOD's lower section is stuck or won't extend",
            "answer": "<p>This almost always happens when the twist-lock is over-tightened or the pod was pushed into the ground while collapsed. To free it: grip the stuck section close to the joint, twist a quarter turn <strong>counter-clockwise</strong> with steady (not sudden) force, and pull gently while twisting. A rubber jar-opener adds grip without scratching. To prevent it: extend fully before staking, and lock each section with a light quarter turn — it doesn't need to be torqued down. Still stuck? <a href=\"/pages/contact-us\">Contact us</a> and we'll make it right.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_1": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What does the Bluetooth remote actually do?",
            "answer": "<p>It's a camera shutter button. Pair it once (Settings → Bluetooth on your phone), open your camera or swing app, and the remote starts/stops video or snaps photos — so you can trigger recording from address instead of running back and forth.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_2": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "The remote won't pair or turn on",
            "answer": "<p>1) Hold the power button 3 seconds until the light blinks. 2) On your phone: Settings → Bluetooth → pair the remote. 3) If it doesn't respond, pull the battery tab or replace the CR2032 battery. 4) Already paired to another phone? \"Forget\" the device and re-pair. Still dead on arrival? <a href=\"/pages/contact-us\">Contact us</a> for a replacement.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_3": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "My phone slides off the magnetic mount",
            "answer": "<p>Magnetic hold depends on what's between the magnet and the phone. Bare iPhone 12+ or MagSafe case: it should snap on firmly and centered — check for dirt on the mount. Non-MagSafe case or Android: use an included 3M metal plate on the outside of the case. Very thick or rugged cases still slipping: put the plate directly on the case surface closest to the mount.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_4": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How do I activate the Sportsbox 3D subscription from my bundle?",
            "answer": "<p>Your activation code and instructions are in the order confirmation email. Download the Sportsbox 3D Golf app, create an account with the <em>same email you used at checkout</em>, and redeem the code under Subscription. Can't find the code? <a href=\"/pages/contact-us\">Contact us</a> with your order number and we'll resend it.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_5": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How do I take the GPUCK / base off to install the spike?",
            "answer": "<p>Hold the base of the unit firmly with one hand and unscrew the GPUCK counter-clockwise with the other. If the puck just spins, grip it flat across its edges (not the rotating head) — a rubber pad helps. The spike then screws into the exposed 1/4 in thread.</p>"
          }
        }
